  "body": "A data URL dedicated worker has an opaque origin. It therefore should not be in the agent cluster of its creator, as that would create a limited information leak.\r\n\r\nHowever, this would mean that a browsing context group can hold agent clusters that do not contain a \"window agent\". This would require adjusting that a bit. Can it later start to hold a \"window agent\" through clever usage of blob URLs? Blob URLs have some same-origin navigation limitations, but do those also apply in noopener type situations? (See also https://github.com/w3c/FileAPI/issues/135.)\r\n\r\nWhile data URLs are not the best use case, eventually we want sandboxing to apply to workers as well, and then this would apply to more URL schemes.\r\n\r\nRelevant for #5210.\r\n\r\n(Realized this while working on https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/21146.)",
